A||||10||DR650SE||How much extra HP with...?||||9||
Z||000000||DR650SE||10-26-2001||02:07 PM||||How much extra horsepower will I get from putting on the ocelot exhaust and sprint performance headers from the fiero store?  I put them on and am working out the other problems in my car so I have yet to test it.  Anyone got numbers?  Thanks for the help.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||9
Z||000001||Turbo88||10-26-2001||02:30 PM||||For the almost 800 bucks you are talking for those parts... you will be much happier with something else. In my opinion, those prices are way way high. You could get someone to custom build you an exhaust system for less than that. <P>That being said, for the same money, you could get new plugs, plug wires, and a coil for the ignition, air better air filter, and add nitrous. With nitrous, you will run circles around what ever you can with just exhaust. If you want to spend some more money, I offer a turbo kit, Archie offers a small block chevy kit, and Triad mentioned building a supercharger kit for the car. <P>But what ever you do, don't spend 800 bucks on an exhaust system that might net you 10-20 hp at the rear wheels. If that......<P>-Bryan<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Turbo88||10-26-2001||02:32 PM||||Another note.. the sprint headers are NOT tuned headers. They might flow better than exhaust manifolds but you won't get the scavanging effect like you would with true equal length tuned headers..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DR650SE||10-26-2001||02:39 PM||||are the sprint headers better then ported manifolds?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Turbo88||10-26-2001||02:51 PM||||for the price? not a chance in hell. they do flow better because there isn't the abrupt turns that the stock manifolds have, but the power gains will be little at best. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||10-26-2001||05:12 PM||||About 10 horsepower for $800 or you could port you manifolds out and put on a high performance muffler for $200 and get the same results. <P>The Sprint Manifolds that the Fierostore sells are not headers; there’re manifolds.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||10-26-2001||05:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DR650SE:<BR><B>are the sprint headers better then ported manifolds?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>According to many, the Sprint manifolds provide about the same gains as ported stock manifolds. They just look a lot sexier.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||DR650SE||10-26-2001||08:58 PM||||Anyone here have the sprint headers?  How do you like them?||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTMike||10-26-2001||09:58 PM||||umm for 800 bucks you could put in a <BR> 3.4 V6.   you can find them as low as 500 bucks. and you would get alot more horse power ||||reg||1
